%S A401421 1,2,3,6,5,6,7,6,12,10,11,18,13,14,15,6,17,24,19,30,21,22,23,18,30,26,
%T A401421 12,42,29,30,31,6,33,34,35,72,37,38,39,30,41,42,43,66,60,46,47,18,56,
%U A401421 60,51,78,53,24,55,42,57,58,59,90,61,62,84,6,65,66,67,102,69,70,71,72
%N A401421 The sum of coreful divisors of n (A284318) that are cubefree (A004709).
%C A401421 The number of these divisors is A323308(n), and the largest of them is A007948(n).
%H A401421 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A401421/b401421.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A401421 Multiplicative with a(p) = p and a(p^e) = p + p^2 for e >= 2.
%F A401421 a(n) = n if n is squarefree (A005117). Nonsquarefree numbers (A013929) k for which a(k) = k are 72, 360, 504, 792, 936, ... . These are the numbers of the form 72*m where m is a 5-rough squarefree number (A276378).
%F A401421 a(n) <= A057723(n), with equality if and only if n is cubefree.
%F A401421 Dirichlet g.f.: zeta(s) * Product_{p prime} (1 + 1/p^(s-1) - 1/p^s + 1/p^(2*s-2)).
%F A401421 Sum_{k=1..n} a(k) ~ n^2 / 2.
%t A401421 f[p_, e_] := If[e == 1, p, p + p^2]; a[1] = 1; a[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; Array[a, 72]
%o A401421 (PARI) a(n) = vecprod([if(f[2] == 1, f[1], f[1] + f[1]^2) | f<-factor(n)~]);
%Y A401421 Cf. A001694, A004709, A005117, A007948, A013929, A057723, A276378, A284318, A323308.
%K A401421 nonn,mult,easy,new
%O A401421 1,2
%A A401421 _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 24 2026
